      "writtenOn": "2025-03-28T09:15:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dirks\u0027 EC doesn\u0027t use power/intel_x86.c so it hasn\u0027t set shutdown reasen `CHIPSET_SHUTDOWN_POWERFAIL`. It doesn\u0027t check `IN_PGOOD_ALL_CORE` which is defined as `PWR_DSW_PWROD` for ADL to set `CHIPSET_SHUTDOWN_POWERFAIL`. I think Dirks probably can\u0027t stop to set AP_IDLE in pb_chipset_shutdown(). board_is_power_good() would be needed for Dirks.\n```\nstatic void pb_chipset_shutdown(void)\n{\n\t/* Don\u0027t set AP_IDLE if shutting down due to power failure. */\n\tif (chipset_get_shutdown_reason() \u003d\u003d CHIPSET_SHUTDOWN_POWERFAIL ||\n\t    !board_is_power_good())\n\t\treturn;\n```",
      "parentUuid": "534b90b4_e2bbdaa6",
      "revId": "59247a4bdab6cbfbb7004e818d8e5f246ea2080b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
